#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542244} :activity/id #uuid "ef3a3edc-d7d1-547d-8515-08949bf0a91c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/id #uuid "8a6eb2f8-5287-523f-8df7-f21c0db8796c" :topic/math-academy-id 6690} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542244 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bfd4a6b-0cff-5025-ac15-1ba07589a334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541606}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541606} :answer-field/id #uuid "c00aedbd-3d32-591a-9238-e662e5a71296" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d6d80b-bee2-5ffe-978c-9a216b9c3522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541538}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541538} :answer-field/id #uuid "7397605e-8fc4-5376-8bac-4c5dbc127439" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77f295d1-1cbb-5b17-a7ef-414238a16c0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334547" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(1) \\\\ y(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{2(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,{e}^{2(t-1)}\\, \\\\ \\,0\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2ec118fb-8e61-556c-8854-cbf857a4c88b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542273}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542252 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "911a0b91-8cfc-5c90-8612-d186b86260d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372705} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7b866a-6af6-5c53-8767-9d73d4a5a6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372706} {:answer/id #uuid "f59f7b97-72d7-544d-92fb-affc25bc255f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372707} {:answer/id #uuid "fba88690-6a3e-517e-b451-20f63869feb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372708} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e0b67b-92e9-576c-93cc-05727469679d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372709}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372706} :answer-field/id #uuid "1879bd9d-054e-59da-ab7b-0aabcf601f7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "981edc7d-4bd0-566a-a596-3fb1014b4ef7" :question/math-academy-id "q-335264" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "488b9d3b-a97f-5cfc-9ee9-56aee87c9e33" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542272}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542267 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372710 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d581ab-eac2-55b5-888d-deaf7a002aed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using properties of $det({Φ}_{0}(0))$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372712} {:answer/id #uuid "813ef154-d604-561e-b48e-0b35325f3927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372713} {:answer/id #uuid "fdaf11ea-4164-580f-829e-d2abaeceb857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372714} {:answer/id #uuid "80ab58cb-932a-566d-b586-c196589d930b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "replacing ${Φ}_{0}(0)$ with ${I}_{n}$ in $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372715}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372715} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4499e16-aabb-5cb2-a67c-ad7557ae05f6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372711} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853ace54-49de-53c0-82ed-cfb835e09e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372717} {:answer/id #uuid "906f3949-ca05-5f13-8b47-f3dce789277e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372718} {:answer/id #uuid "9c8541f4-adab-5b02-9915-46d4efed7ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using diagonalization of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372719} {:answer/id #uuid "167e465a-c594-58b2-a782-69d90ccc3a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372717} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0cfc463-a00c-5a02-b25e-b6454e6a70ed" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "484d762f-5acf-5df4-8df4-94cc90a1d4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372722} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e78e24-6079-5e65-a2d8-6a25635330b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of a solution curve" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372723} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddac18e-8996-5267-a9f1-7a3b6bca18c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of the determinant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372724} {:answer/id #uuid "12142844-889a-5ee2-b9bb-a31bbc51020a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372722} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dea9463-8880-5a50-ac39-82e4de0d8f50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "da2b3537-4a89-5afc-8ad7-721d1c3c30a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-336480" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, any solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ From $\\text{L2}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nEvaluating this identity at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is precisely line $\\text{L3}.$ Thus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we know\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Replacing ${Φ}_{0}(0)$ with ${I}_{n}$ in the equation $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{replacing }{Φ}_{0}(0)\\text{ with }{I}_{n}\\text{ in }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$"} :step/id #uuid "845477bd-8d9d-58e3-9bf9-2073bbad3f86"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542272 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311564 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f8dc2a-d1c1-50ad-9080-e4aea1133091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{3(t-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308761}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308761} :answer-field/id #uuid "93eace97-bb5c-5bd2-b8df-7eca81320545" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07bdd633-a0bf-5ddf-ac96-58b9d4b0f277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(t-2){e}^{3(t-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308806}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308806} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6cac817-7eaa-5d9c-919e-8afb3c166bfa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "80bead61-fb6c-5bf6-88d2-511e52d01763" :question/math-academy-id "q-335273" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-2)} & (t-2){e}^{3(t-2)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-2)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,(t-2){e}^{3(t-2)}\\, \\\\ \\,{e}^{3(t-2)}\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "940a38de-c4fa-51fc-b135-2a4dcc4b60cf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542267}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542273 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359dac84-023f-5ac4-b1e5-2b024191e8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541532} {:answer/id #uuid "557ae54f-10b2-58ab-9e71-0c628ea5f179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541593} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4ad265-f473-5a67-8913-d792566b24af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541815} {:answer/id #uuid "d11ef4d7-b160-5577-b380-46de80da0930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541866} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c0af83-088a-5ec4-9706-445e6d105d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541932}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541932} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94becd7-b475-5661-836a-13b2396bb899" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ebc3a86d-4663-502d-a702-2a2557f07e8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334779" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=8y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-8x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"} :step/id #uuid "a176a8d0-ae3d-5337-b4e5-e954a5e68792" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542252}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541425}]}
